WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.480
<b>Imperial Capital</b>

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:41.280
Nobody told me they'd be this strong!

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:45.500
Kento!

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:46.870
C'mon, get up!

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:48.240
They're gonna catch up to us!

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.760
I know, I know!

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:17.280
Wow...

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:20.500
Are you all right?

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.040
Y-Yes...

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:30.250
Thank you so much for your help.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.920
Think nothing of it.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.530
To provide help for those 
who need it is my creed.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:38.720
<i>It would appear...</i>

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.610
<i>that they have only just 
set out on their journey.</i>

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:45.080
<i>It reminds me of when I left my homeland.</i>

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:52.230
Aren't you the three boys 
who came to Nekoya before?

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.340
Huh?!

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.920
I'm on my way there now. 
Would you care to join me?

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:56.730
Yeah!

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.190
But we don't have any money.

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:01.740
Oh, yeah...

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.990
Please, you need not worry about money.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:08.150
I'll pay for the three of you.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:10.210
All right!

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.750
Welcome!

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.120
Oh?

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.210
You four are all here together?

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:22.330
Indeed. I just happened to run 
into Jack and his friends.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.840
It's been a long time.

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:25.810
It's great to see you again!

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:29.850
You three haven't been here in quite 
a while. Did something happen?

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.390
We became adventurers!

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:35.650
Adventurers? So you're on a journey?

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:40.270
Yes, we were in a forest in the 
empire that's said to be haunted.

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:42.660
We were trying to find 
what's behind the rumor...

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:45.660
But we were chased off by wraiths.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.420
And then Tatsu—

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:50.050
Teriyaki Chicken-san saved you?

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:51.160
Tatsu?

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.710
Yeah! He was super strong!

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:56.570
He was like, slash, bash, crash!

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:58.550
Uh...

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:01.850
You know what they say about 
fighting on an empty stomach.

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:04.540
Now, why don't you show us to our table?

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:09.460
I'll come back when you're ready to order.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.510
It's been a few years since 
I picked up this menu.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:19.710
I'll have my usual teriyaki 
chicken with seishu—

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.450
Hm? What's this?

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.450
Teriyaki burger?

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:29.020
We've never ordered that before, have we?

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:31.690
Yeah, we always just get hamburgers.

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:34.360
I've been curious about 
it for a while, though.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:37.250
Hmm... Judging by the name,

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:41.320
it seems like it should be 
similar to teriyaki chicken...

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:45.050
Excuse me, waitress. May I have a moment?

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:45.900
Of course.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:52.270
What sort of dish is this teriyaki burger?

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:55.620
The teriyaki burger is 
made with sliced oranie,

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:58.910
lelesa, and a white sauce 
called "mayonnaise,"

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.030
on top of a hamburger patty 
coated in teriyaki sauce

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.180
and placed between two slices of bread.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.840
Ah, that sounds quite tasty.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:09.420
Then I'll have the teriyaki burger,

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:12.200
and a cold tea to drink, please.

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:14.540
Me, too! I'll have the same!

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.000
With cola to drink!

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.090
Me, too!

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:18.280
Same for me.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.210
Your order has been accepted.

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:26.340
I can't wait to see what it's gonna be like!

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:28.190
Indeed.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:30.920
Um, if I can ask you something 
totally unrelated...

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:33.930
You wear the garments of the western 
continent, and wield a single-edged sword.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.730
Could it be that you're...

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:38.310
Ah, I neglected to introduce myself.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:40.900
My name is Tatsugoro.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.520
I knew it!

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.490
T-Tatsugoro?!

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.260
The samurai master?!

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.110
What?! You're super famous!

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:53.190
I had no idea you were a 
regular at this restaurant.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:58.020
And I never would have guessed the 
mischievous boys I happened to see

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:00.630
at the Restaurant to Another 
World had become adventurers.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:07.550
Hey, I heard you slew a hundred manticores 
in a single night! Is that true?

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.550
No, that's not true!

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:12.720
What? It's not?

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:17.200
No. I believe the number 
I slew that night was eight.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:21.190
It's still incredible that you 
could kill eight by yourself.

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:25.390
The songs of the bards 
are far too exaggerated.

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:30.800
But you were so heroic 
when you saved us today!

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:34.740
I can see why the bards would 
want to sing about you!

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:40.330
You have the skills to defeat wraiths 
without using prayers or sorcery.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:44.460
Well, the truth is, I use a 
certain trick to kill wraiths.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:45.530
Huh?

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.160
Long ago, I had an elf imbue 
this katana with magic

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:53.100
that would allow it to cut beings 
that are not of this world.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:58.180
That means it can even slay 
things like spirits and ghosts.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.820
I get it!

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:03.110
Please tell us stories of your travels!

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:04.400
I want to hear them, too!

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.730
Me, too!

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:09.690
In that case, here's a tale 
from when I was still young,

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:12.450
shortly after I departed from my homeland...

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:20.870
<i>Teriyaki Burger</i>

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:18.580
Thank you for waiting.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.880
Here are your teriyaki burgers and drinks.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:23.880
This looks great!

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:28.000
<i>Hmm... This does look like a 
dish I can expect to enjoy.</i>

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:32.630
Well, let's eat before they get cold.

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:42.020
So good!

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:44.380
Now for me.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.280
Delicious!

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.780
<i>I usually only have rice,</i>

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:52.780
<i>but bread is delicious, too!</i>

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:58.290
<i>The oranie has a sharp crunch, 
and the lelesa is crispy.</i>

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:02.790
<i>The sweet and sour teriyaki sauce 
and the tangy mayonnaise...</i>

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:06.850
<i>Having both of them together 
gives depth to the flavor.</i>

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:09.800
<i>The hint of spice in the oranie 
works very well with it, too.</i>

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:16.550
<i>The sauce is a bit thicker than the 
sauce on the teriyaki chicken.</i>

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:19.680
<i>Hmm... Perhaps it's this thickness</i>

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:22.640
<i>that makes the teriyaki sauce 
coat the meat so well.</i>

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:26.670
<i>No wonder it doesn't lose any flavor, 
even when eaten with vegetables.</i>

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.810
<i>And the tenderness of the meat is exquisite.</i>

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:34.600
<i>With every bite, the juices 
blend with the teriyaki sauce</i>

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:37.570
<i>to create a flavor that makes me want more.</i>

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:43.080
<i>The crispy fried cobbler's 
tubers are great, as well.</i>

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:53.470
<i>The teriyaki burger is delicious. 
It is delicious, but...</i>

00:08:58.600 --> 00:08:59.850
Sir...

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.600
Yes? What is it?

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.820
The bun on the teriyaki burger can 
be made with rice instead of bread.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:07.100
Would you like to try that?

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.570
Rice? Then I will have—

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.610
I wanna try that, too!

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:14.860
For all of us, please.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.480
Understood.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:22.370
Thank you for waiting. Here are 
your teriyaki rice burgers.

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:26.020
I'm thinking of adding this to the menu.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:28.310
Ah, this does look tasty!

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:29.740
All right, let's eat!

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:30.770
Yeah!

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:35.630
Delicious!

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:40.890
The savory crunch of the grilled 
rice stimulates my appetite!

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:45.890
The sweet and salty sauce goes 
perfectly with the rice!

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:49.650
The rice has a more satisfying 
texture than the bread.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.050
Yeah!

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:53.330
It's a totally different 
flavor than the bread.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:59.910
<i>Yes, the rice I'm used to eating 
with teriyaki just feels right.</i>

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:03.160
<i>I bet it would go well with seishu, too!</i>

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:05.690
That was so good!

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:09.250
Hamburgers are great, but I 
like teriyaki burgers, too!

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:12.040
For sure! It was even better with rice!

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:15.170
I can't decide which one 
I should eat next time I'm here!

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:20.970
<i>If I had sons... rather, grandsons... 
I wonder if they would be like this.</i>

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:25.220
<i>If I ever run into them again, 
I'll bring them back here.</i>

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:39.490
Well, Demon Lord, 
this concludes today's duties.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.320
Thank you for such wonderful work.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:43.790
Yes, thank you, as well.

00:10:54.310 --> 00:10:57.260
<i>"Demon Lord," huh?</i>

00:10:57.480 --> 00:11:01.210
<i>The previous demon lord, my mother, Altina,</i>

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:07.030
<i>swore fealty to the previous emperor, 
Wilhelm, about fifty years ago,</i>

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:09.600
<i>and became a retainer in 
service to the empire.</i>

00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:13.130
<i>She was given a territory within 
the empire to reign over,</i>

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:16.560
<i>giving all the demons who had lived 
in shame before a place of their own.</i>

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:18.220
<i>She was truly great.</i>

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:23.030
<i>Seven magnificent horns grew 
on her head like a crown.</i>

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:27.040
<i>She had great wings that 
allowed her to fly at will.</i>

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:30.410
<i>A lash of her powerful tail
 could cut through iron.</i>

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:35.090
<i>And she possessed magic surpassing 
even that of the elves.</i>

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:39.010
<i>Compared to her, my horn is so small</i>

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:42.430
<i>that it's always hidden under my bangs.</i>

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:48.100
<i>My wings are like a bat's, so underdeveloped 
that they can't even lift me.</i>

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.680
<i>My tiny tail doesn't even reach my knees.</i>

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:56.230
<i>And my magic is only about as 
powerful as a human sorcerer's.</i>

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:02.200
<i>Am I really worthy of being 
called a demon lord?</i>

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:09.170
Lionel, with his undefeated 
record in the arena,

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:11.380
would make a much better demon lord.

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:14.000
Huh?

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.750
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:18.900
What in the world...

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:26.260
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:26.260
If it's dangerous, I'll have 
to deal with it appropriately.

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:33.270
It almost looks like one of 
the demon capital's taverns.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:37.160
So many different races 
are here eating together.

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:38.840
What a strange place.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.280
Wait, isn't that...

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:45.370
That was so good!

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:44.780
Lionel?!

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.030
Thanks for the meal!

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.910
I'll leave the money here!

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:50.660
Thank you very much.

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:55.120
Demon Lord Lastina!

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.070
Hello, Lionel.

00:12:57.070 --> 00:12:59.420
So, um... what is this place?

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:01.270
The Restaurant to Another World.

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:04.180
Another world? This is another world?

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:05.470
It is.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:09.070
The food is great. You should 
have some before you go.

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:11.930
Well, I'll be on my way now.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:19.250
He said I should eat something, 
but what should I...

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:21.930
Are you Demon Lord Lastina?

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:26.700
Princess Adelheid?!

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:32.200
I heard you were undergoing 
treatment for an illness.

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:33.630
Why have you come here?

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:37.050
My grandfather suggested it.

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:38.500
Suggested?

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:41.370
Would you like to join me?

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:45.720
Shareef and Renner aren't here today...

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:49.120
<i>Does she mean the prince and 
princess of the Land of Sand?</i>

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.270
How about it?

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:52.610
I will, then.

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:56.350
Welcome!

00:13:57.420 --> 00:13:59.600
Wow, you have such magnificent goat horns.

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:02.050
M-Magnificent?

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:05.360
That's the first time anyone's 
ever complimented my horns!

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:10.370
I have a horn, but it's so small,
 my bangs cover it.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:13.370
Oh, what a cute horn!

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:16.980
I mean, uh... This is your 
first time here, isn't it?

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:18.320
Oh, yes.

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:20.710
Can you read the eastern 
continent's language?

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:22.210
Yes, of course.

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.060
Here's our menu!

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:25.700
Thank you.

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:29.650
There are so many things on this menu.

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:31.330
Which should I have?

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:35.640
If you can't decide, 
may I recommend a parfait?

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.640
A... parfait?

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.400
They're sweet and very delicious.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:44.790
There are several different 
types of parfaits, too.

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:48.900
If I recall correctly, you're not very 
fond of fruit, correct?

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:51.500
I'm impressed you remember that.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.020
You're right. I do enjoy sweet foods,

00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:56.160
but I'm not fond of fruit.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:59.180
In that case, do you like kaffa?

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:01.640
I thought Shareef said he gave you some,

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:05.550
and you took quite a liking to it.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:06.660
Kaffa?

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:10.180
Yes, I do enjoy kaffa.

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:11.670
In that case...

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:13.630
Excuse me, Kuro?

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:16.060
Yes?

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:20.520
A mocha chocolate parfait for 
Demon Lord Lastina, please.

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:23.910
And can I change my order 
for a chocolate parfait

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:27.310
to a mocha chocolate parfait instead?

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:29.250
Please wait one moment.

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:34.320
Master, can you change a chocolate 
parfait to a mocha chocolate parfait?

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:37.880
That will be fine.

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:41.330
Please change it to a mocha 
chocolate parfait, then.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:42.860
Understood.

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:47.590
By the way, how did you get 
here, Demon Lord Lastina?

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:51.980
Well, I found a strange door 
in my private chambers,

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.470
and it led here.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:56.470
Oh! What amazing luck!

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.470
Um... what do you mean by that?

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:03.310
There's no way to know where 
a new door might appear.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:06.590
You're very fortunate to have one 
appear in your private chambers!

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:08.170
I see...

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:10.740
Yes, this is a wonderful place!

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.720
I'm certain you will love it, too.

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:18.740
I see. That is reassuring.

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:23.330
You're finally smiling, Demon Lord Lastina.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:24.750
I'm so glad.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:25.630
Huh?

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.730
Aside from being wary of this place,

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:31.750
it seemed as if something was bothering you.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.790
Did something happen?

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:40.220
Why don't you tell me about it,
 if you don't mind?

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:41.750
But...

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:47.230
<i>Mocha Chocolate Parfait</i>

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.400
Thank you for waiting.

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:47.230
Here are your mocha chocolate parfaits.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:49.370
My, it looks delicious!

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:51.260
Shall we eat our parfaits first?

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:52.110
Sure.

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:57.120
It's delicious!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.140
<i>This is a mocha chocolate parfait?</i>

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:03.250
<i>It certainly is arranged beautifully,</i>

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.210
<i>but it is quite dark... and brown.</i>

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:07.130
<i>Is it burnt?</i>

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:10.840
The mocha chocolate parfait 
is delicious, too!

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:15.090
<i>But Princess Adelheid certainly 
seems to be enjoying it.</i>

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:17.150
<i>And this is another world,</i>

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:19.850
<i>so maybe something like 
this could taste good.</i>

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:25.170
Try yours, Demon Lord Lastina.

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:26.850
A-All right...

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:34.480
<i>Oh! It's delicious!</i>

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.470
<i>It's not overly sweet,</i>

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:38.920
<i>but the crunchy texture is irresistible!</i>

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:44.370
<i>And next...</i>

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:46.870
<i>This must be the chocolate.</i>

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:49.860
<i>It's bitter?</i>

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:52.530
<i>Wait... it's sweet, too?!</i>

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:57.700
<i>I get it. This bitterness is why 
the princess asked me about kaffa.</i>

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:00.280
<i>It's not quite the same as kaffa,</i>

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:02.890
<i>but it's deeply aromatic and tastes great.</i>

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:09.030
<i>Is this white stuff milk?</i>

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:13.900
<i>The mellow fragrance of milk is filling 
my mouth, and it's mildly sweet, too.</i>

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:28.400
<i>The dark substance drizzled on top 
appears to be melted chocolate.</i>

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:33.460
<i>And now there's something cold!</i>

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:36.260
<i>The texture changed?!</i>

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:39.300
<i>It's firmer than the milk 
confection I had a moment ago.</i>

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:47.220
<i>It's sweet with a hint of bitterness, 
but not like the bitterness from before.</i>

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:51.960
<i>Of course! This is kaffa!</i>

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:57.980
<i>So this dessert is made by mixing lots of 
sugar and milk into kaffa and freezing it!</i>

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:02.560
<i>A bread-like confection that 
bursts with the flavor of kaffa,</i>

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:05.780
<i>and a confection that softly 
melts in the mouth...</i>

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:11.080
<i>There are so many different flavors and 
textures to enjoy in a single glass!</i>

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:14.310
<i>What a luxurious thing this parfait is!</i>

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:20.590
<i>And last is this jiggly part 
that looks like slime.</i>

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:26.360
<i>It's kaffa that's been solidified!</i>

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:30.600
<i>It feels smooth on my tongue and 
slides so easily down my throat!</i>

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:41.610
That was delicious!

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:46.680
I'm so glad you enjoyed it.

00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:51.120
Kuro.

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:55.320
Two cups of hot café au lait, please.

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:57.630
Very well.

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:02.430
Thank you for waiting. 
Here is your café au lait.

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:05.890
Please tell me what's troubling you,
 Demon Lord Lastina.

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:09.210
All right, since you asked...

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:15.900
The truth is, I've been questioning whether 
I should really be the demon lord.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:21.740
I feel there are other, stronger demons
 more worthy of the title.

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:23.910
Oh, is that so?

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:28.420
My father said he found it reassuring

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:31.120
that you were the new demon lord.

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:33.120
The emperor said that?

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:34.320
Yes.

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:36.940
He said that since you became demon lord,

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:40.570
both tax revenue and population 
have increased in our domain.

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:43.130
He said you were a fine negotiator, too.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:44.630
But...

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:51.330
Unfortunately, I'm just too... 
well... weak to be a demon lord.

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:54.180
Is there a problem with being weak?

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:55.020
What?

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:59.410
I can't even use a dagger, 
much less a sword,

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:01.250
but I'm still a princess.

00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:05.040
My father only has modest knowledge 
of the sword, too,

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:06.550
but he's still the emperor.

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:12.540
I don't think it's absolutely 
necessary for a ruler to be strong.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.800
Besides, if you are weak,

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:18.460
there's just no need for you 
to fight in any battles.

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:23.800
I think you simply need to be 
the demon lord in your own way.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:26.370
My own way...

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:29.550
You're right!

00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:30.790
Yes!

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:37.970
I'm glad I came here.

00:21:44.080 --> 00:21:48.460
By the way, what is your relationship 
with Prince Shareef and Princess Renner?

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:52.260
They're friends I met here at the 
Restaurant to Another World.

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:54.870
Princess Renner is a pleasure to talk to,

00:21:54.870 --> 00:22:00.210
and Prince Shareef is someone 
I always feel happy dining with.

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:03.120
Wow! Please tell me more!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:41.940
<i>Quiche</i>

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:50.250
<i>Coffee Float</i>
